rules:
Unit tests (`.claude/rules/unit-test-admission.md`): each case guards a distinct failure mode, and its docstring names the mutant that turns it red ("Mutant: ... -- red"), as `test_exl3_ram_prefetch_step.py` does. Put new cases in existing files:
- table and service cases in `test/registered/unit/layers/moe/test_ram_prefetch_tables.py`, which keeps `test_each_row_targets_the_next_consecutive_layer_with_a_biased_gate` unchanged;
- launch-gate cases in `test/registered/unit/test_expert_stream_requirements_exl3.py`, using its `_launch`/`_gate`/`CPU_EXPERTS_ENV` helpers;
- the L+2 staleness and pool-lifetime case in `test/registered/unit/kernels/test_exl3_ram_prefetch_gpu_host.py`, using `prefetch_rig(tmp_path, rows=3)` with `enable_gpu(rig, targets=torch.tensor([[2,0],[-1,-1],[-1,-1]]))` and `write_candidate_slot`, and driving records of rows 0, 1 and 2 through `rig.sim.post`/`rig.host.pump`/`spec_pump`/`forced`.

`both_cpu_ab.py`: add `"SGLANG_DSV41_RAM_PREFETCH_HORIZON": "1"` to a pin dict merged into every arm, the same way `IDLE_DRIVE_OFF` is applied by a loop. Define `dspark-both-prefetch-gpu-misscut-idle2-l2` after that loop as `{**ARMS["dspark-both-prefetch-gpu-misscut-idle2"][0], "SGLANG_DSV41_RAM_PREFETCH_HORIZON": "2", "SGLANG_DSV41_RAM_PREFETCH_MARGIN_FLOORS": ""}`, with dspark True, a one-line comment and `REFERENCE[...] = "dspark-both-misscut"`. In `test_both_cpu_ab.py`:
- add the arm to `IDLE2_ARMS`;
- add one test that it differs from idle2 in the horizon alone and that floors are "";
- add one test that every other arm pins horizon 1 against an exported shell.

